@startuml Agent Interactions
title Agent Interaction Patterns

package "DM Agent" {
    component [Scenario Generation] as ScenGen
    component [Action Resolution] as ActRes
    component [Round Synthesis] as RndSyn
    component [Round Summary] as RndSum
    component [Mission Debrief] as Debrief
}

package "Player Agent" {
    component [Action Declaration] as PlayerAct
    component [Intent Analysis] as Intent
    component [Combat Actions] as PlayerCombat
}

package "Enemy Agent" {
    component [Tactical Analysis] as EnemyTac
    component [Target Selection] as EnemyTgt
    component [Combat Actions] as EnemyCombat
}

package "NPC Agent" {
    component [Simple Actions] as NPCAct
    note right of NPCAct
        Limited action set:
        - flee, hide, plead
        - comply, dialogue
        - assist, pass
        (NO attack/tactical)
    end note
}

package "Shared State" {
    database [Character States] as CharState
    database [Combat State] as CombatState
    database [Scene Clocks] as Clocks
    database [Environment] as Env
}

package "Mechanics Engine" {
    component [Damage Processing] as Damage
    component [Void Processing] as Void
    component [Roll Calculation] as Rolls
    component [Effect Application] as Effects
}

' DM interactions
ScenGen --> Env : sets void_level
ScenGen --> CombatState : spawns enemies
RndSyn --> CharState : reads all states
RndSyn --> Clocks : reads/updates
ActRes --> Damage : extracts from narration
ActRes --> Void : extracts from narration
ActRes --> Effects : declares effects

' Player interactions
PlayerAct --> CharState : reads own state
PlayerAct --> CombatState : reads targets
Intent ..> PlayerAct : informs
PlayerCombat ..> PlayerAct : implements
PlayerAct --> ActRes : sends action
ActRes --> Damage : processes
ActRes --> CharState : updates

' Enemy interactions
EnemyTac --> CombatState : analyzes threats
EnemyTgt --> CharState : selects targets
EnemyCombat --> ActRes : sends action
ActRes --> Damage : processes
ActRes --> CharState : updates

' NPC interactions
NPCAct --> CharState : reads own state
NPCAct --> ActRes : sends simple action
ActRes --> CharState : updates (if not pass)

' Mechanics flow
ActRes --> Effects : declares
Effects --> Damage : applies
Effects --> Void : applies
Effects --> Rolls : validates
Damage --> CharState : updates HP/wounds
Void --> CharState : updates void_score
Effects --> Clocks : updates ticks

note top of ScenGen
    DM Phase 1: Generate scenario
    - Theme, location
    - Initial void_level
    - Spawn initial enemies
    - Set starting clocks
end note

note top of RndSyn
    DM Phase 2: Synthesize round
    - Entity conversions (NPC ↔ Enemy)
    - Clock updates
    - Environmental changes
    - Story advancement
end note

note top of ActRes
    DM Phase 3: Resolve actions
    - Narrate outcome
    - Declare mechanical effects
    - Extract damage/void/etc
    - Update character states
end note

note top of RndSum
    DM Phase 4: Summarize round
    - Tactical situation
    - Story developments
    - Clock status
end note

note bottom of CharState
    Authoritative state:
    - HP, wounds, stun
    - Void score
    - Soul credits
    - Status effects
end note

note bottom of Clocks
    Bidirectional clocks:
    - Progress (0→max)
    - Countdown (max→0)
    - Per-round tick rates
end note

@enduml
